# Repo-root Docker build context (apps/web depends on packages/api-client, so its
# build context must include both - see apps/web/Dockerfile). Without this, a locally
# present node_modules or build output collides with what the image itself installs/builds,
# and - since the context is now the whole repo, not just apps/web - secrets nested
# anywhere in the tree (infra/.env, apps/web/.env.local, TLS keys, local tool config)
# would otherwise reach the Docker daemon. Patterns must match nested paths, not just
# repo-root files: `.env` only excludes the root file, `**/.env` excludes every one.
.git
.claude
.mcp.json
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

infra/certs

**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/.turbo
**/.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo

# Backend build/venv output - irrelevant to the web image but sizable, and not excluded
# by the patterns above.
**/target
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.egg-info

.specs
docs
